    "summary": "Shipped and smoke-checked; everything recorded in docs/epics/complete-consistent-richer-code-index-one-E20261011c2ba6fa6/S011/smoke.md (commit 284ce2c4). Pushed main @99c6a8df (after two --no-ff merges of other sessions' work, each swept, see S011/sweeps.md). Installed daemon updated to 99c6a8df via the update() service function and restarted; the old daemon (pid 57247) hung after logging 'bye' (pid file and socket removed, process alive, ignored SIGTERM, MDB_LOCK_FAILURE in its log), was SIGKILLed, and startDaemon() brought up pid 81990 on 99c6a8df. The user restarted every client session; afterwards the only MCP server is pid 87098 started 11:59:44 (after the update). Smoke 1: insrc_analyze one-shot through the restarted session returned a full grounded bundle (M, 34 files, model=opus). Smoke 2: an issue workflow run started through pid 87098 (emit_plan), continued through a NEW installed MCP process pid 88099 (plan -> emit_step s1, new token), and continued again through pid 87098 (s1 -> emit_step s2); abandoned, nothing written. Smoke 3: lsof shows only the daemon (81990) on ~/.insrc/graph.lmdb and graph.lmdb-lock; no process held anything under ~/.insrc/lance at that moment; no other node process (MCP server included) has a store path open. These are smoke checks that need the running installed daemon and a person restarting sessions, so they are reported, not run by the gate.",
